.TH NEDMAIL 1
.SH NAME
nedmail \- reading mail
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B upas/nedmail
[
.B -f
.I mailbox
] [
.B -m
.I name
]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.I Nedmail
is an interactive command-line mail reader, after Plan 9's
.IR nedmail .
It is a client of
.IR upas/fs (1):
it lists the numbered message directories a mailbox presents under
.BR /mail/fs ,
reads each message's parsed
.B info
and its content files, and deletes through
.BR /mail/fs/ctl .
.PP
If
.B /mail/fs
is not already being served and
.B -f
names a Unix mbox file,
.I nedmail
starts
.IR upas/fs (1)
on it first.
.B -m
selects the mailbox name to read (default
.BR mbox ).
.PP
At the prompt, which shows the current message number, a line is
.IB address command " " args
where either part may be omitted: a bare
.I address
prints that message and a bare newline advances to the next one.
.SS Addresses
.TP
.I n
message number
.TP
.B .
the current message
.TP
.B $
the last message
.TP
.B ^
the first message
.TP
.BI + n
.I n
messages forward (default 1)
.TP
.BI - n
.I n
messages back
.TP
.BI / regexp /
the next message whose from, subject or to matches
.SS Commands
.TP
.B p
print the message (a short header block, then the decoded body)
.TP
.B P
print the raw message
.TP
.B "\(dq"
print the body quoted with a leading attribution
.TP
.B h
print a one-line summary of the message
.TP
.B b
print summaries of the next ten messages
.TP
.B H
print the message's MIME structure
.TP
.B d
mark the message for deletion
.TP
.B u
remove the deletion mark
.TP
.B =
print the message number
.TP
.BI w " file"
save the decoded body to
.I file
.TP
.BI s " file"
append the raw message to
.I file
(as an mbox)
.TP
.B y
.PD 0
.TP
.B i
resynchronise with the mailbox, picking up new mail
.PD
.TP
.B q
quit, deleting the marked messages from the mailbox
.TP
.B x
quit without deleting anything
.TP
.B help
print a command summary
.SH EXAMPLE
Read an mbox, delete the second message, and quit:
.EX

	% upas/nedmail -f /tmp/mbox
	3 messages
	1: 2
	...
	2: d
	2: q
	deleted 1 message

.EE
.SH SOURCE
.B /appl/cmd/upas/nedmail.b
.SH SEE ALSO
.IR upas/fs (1),
.IR upas-fetch (1),
.IR upas-send (1)
.SH BUGS
This is the reader core. Reply and forward
.RB ( r ,
.BR R ,
.BR a ,
.BR m ,
.BR M ),
the pipe and shell escapes
.RB ( \(ba ,
.BR \(ba\(ba ,
.BR ! )
and message filing
.RB ( f )
are not yet implemented; they await the
.I marshal
milestone (see
.BR doc/upas-plan.md ).
